WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:02.300
-It is time for
our latest installment

00:00:02.300 --> 00:00:03.801
of "Tonight Show Polls."
Here we go.

00:00:03.801 --> 00:00:08.400
-♪ "Tonight Show Polls" ♪

00:00:10.334 --> 00:00:11.801
-Let's check out
this first poll.

00:00:11.801 --> 00:00:13.734
This poll asked,
"If you're a parent,

00:00:13.734 --> 00:00:15.734
how are you handling
school closings?"

00:00:15.734 --> 00:00:18.167
50% said, "Getting my kids
set up on Zoom."

00:00:18.167 --> 00:00:20.767
30% said, "In-person tutoring."

00:00:20.767 --> 00:00:23.300
And 20% said, "Wine."
[ Laughter ]

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:25.300
That's not the only --

00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:27.100
Surprised it's that low.
-That would do it, yeah.

00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:29.467
-The next poll asked,
"How are you testing for COVID?"

00:00:29.467 --> 00:00:32.167
64% said, "Using at-home
rapid tests."

00:00:32.167 --> 00:00:35.400
32% said, "Getting a PCR
at my doctor's office."

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:37.634
4% said, "Shoving a Q-tip
up my nose,

00:00:37.634 --> 00:00:40.033
rubbing it on a pregnancy test,
and hoping for the best."

00:00:40.033 --> 00:00:41.767
[ Applause ]

00:00:41.767 --> 00:00:43.634
-Florida.
-[ Chuckles ]

00:00:45.234 --> 00:00:47.667
This next poll said, "What are
you watching on Netflix?"

00:00:47.667 --> 00:00:49.467
10% said, "Queer Eye."

00:00:49.467 --> 00:00:51.367
10% said, "Emily in Paris."

00:00:51.367 --> 00:00:54.100
80% said, "My own reflection
while I scroll through TikTok."

00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:57.767
[ Laughter ]

00:00:57.767 --> 00:01:00.801
[ Chuckles ]

00:01:00.801 --> 00:01:01.868
This next one asked,

00:01:01.868 --> 00:01:03.601
"How did you feel
after your booster shot?"

00:01:03.601 --> 00:01:05.434
50% said, "I felt normal."

00:01:05.434 --> 00:01:07.634
49% said,
"I felt a little achy."

00:01:07.634 --> 00:01:10.067
The CEO of Pfizer said,
"I pfelt perpfectly pfine."

00:01:10.067 --> 00:01:12.467
[ Laughter ]

00:01:14.901 --> 00:01:16.901
This next one asked,
"What's the best way to make

00:01:16.901 --> 00:01:19.133
your home entertainment system
feel like a movie theater?"

00:01:19.133 --> 00:01:21.300
12% said, "Get a widescreen TV."

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:23.901
23% said,
"Buy a comfortable recliner."

00:01:23.901 --> 00:01:26.801
65% said, "Hire a stranger
to sit next to you

00:01:26.801 --> 00:01:28.501
and suck on a Milk Dud
too loudly."

00:01:28.501 --> 00:01:32.000
[ Laughter, applause ]

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:34.067
-[ Sucking loudly ]

00:01:34.067 --> 00:01:36.801
-[ Chuckles ]

00:01:36.801 --> 00:01:38.334
You likin' the movie?

00:01:38.334 --> 00:01:39.501
[ Laughter ]

00:01:39.501 --> 00:01:41.133
-Can I have one of those?
-Sure.

00:01:41.133 --> 00:01:42.901
-[ Imitates splattering ]
-There you go.

00:01:42.901 --> 00:01:44.634
-I got two packs.
-[ Chuckles ]

00:01:44.634 --> 00:01:46.434
Every time we would
go out to the movies,

00:01:46.434 --> 00:01:48.300
my mom,
she would sneak in candy.

00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:50.467
And it was just like
the loudest candy

00:01:50.467 --> 00:01:51.834
you could ever sneak in
anywhere.

00:01:51.834 --> 00:01:54.033
It was just like wrapping
and unwrapping and wrapping.

00:01:54.033 --> 00:01:55.367
And I'd go,
"What is your thing?"

00:01:55.367 --> 00:01:57.133
And then all of a sudden
I heard her go like...

00:01:57.133 --> 00:01:58.934
[ Hissing ]

00:01:58.934 --> 00:02:01.834
She had, like, a 2-liter bottle
of seltzer or something.

00:02:01.834 --> 00:02:05.334
[ Laughter ]
"What are you doing?"

00:02:05.334 --> 00:02:07.267
-Saving money, man.

00:02:07.267 --> 00:02:08.601
-How do you like your burger?
-Are you cooking stuff?

00:02:08.601 --> 00:02:11.234
-Yeah. How do you like
your burger? Medium?

00:02:11.234 --> 00:02:14.601
-I got a fondue pot for nachos.
-[ Chuckles ]

00:02:14.601 --> 00:02:17.300
This next poll asked, Have you
played the new game Wordle?

00:02:17.300 --> 00:02:18.934
Isn't it so much fun?"

00:02:18.934 --> 00:02:20.801
25% said, "M-A-Y-B-E."

00:02:20.801 --> 00:02:22.734
25% said, "G-R-A-V-E."

00:02:22.734 --> 00:02:24.334
25% said, "A-G-A-V-E.

00:02:24.334 --> 00:02:26.000
25% said, "A-G-R-E-E."

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:26.901
Yeah, we did it!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:26.901 --> 00:02:29.567
♪♪

00:02:31.434 --> 00:02:33.734
This next poll asks, "What
rating would you give

00:02:33.734 --> 00:02:35.334
The Weeknd's new album?"

00:02:35.334 --> 00:02:37.400
100% said, "Tn out of tn."

00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:40.100
[ Laughter ]

00:02:40.100 --> 00:02:42.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:42.567 --> 00:02:44.000
That was a thinker kind of,
yeah.

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:45.501
-A thinker, not a stinker.

00:02:45.501 --> 00:02:48.501
-The last polls asked,
"What angers you the most?"

00:02:48.501 --> 00:02:50.033
60% said, "Politics."

00:02:50.033 --> 00:02:51.634
39% said, "Taxes."

00:02:51.634 --> 00:02:53.601
Elmo said,
"Rocks can't eat cookies."

00:02:53.601 --> 00:02:54.801
There you go, everybody.

00:02:54.801 --> 00:02:56.467
That's all we have for
"Tonight Show Polls."

